{
  "_id": "tg-weary",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Rebekah said to Isaac, I am weary of my life, Gen. 27:46. smote … until his hand was weary, 2 Sam. 23:10. neither be weary of his correction, Prov. 3:11. labour of the foolish wearieth every one, Eccl. 10:15. new moons and your appointed feasts … I am weary to bear them, Isa. 1:14. None shall be weary nor stumble, Isa. 5:27 (2 Ne. 15:26). will ye weary my God also, Isa. 7:13 (2 Ne. 17:13). rest wherewith ye may cause the weary to rest, Isa. 28:12. shall run, and not be weary, Isa. 40:31 (D&C 89:20). Thou art wearied in the multitude of thy counsels, Isa. 47:13. Thou art wearied in the greatness of thy way, Isa. 57:10. they … weary themselves to commit iniquity, Jer. 9:5. Ye have wearied the Lord with your words, Mal. 2:17.",
